0	105	Franz Fischler (born 23 September 1946) is an Austrian politician from the Austrian People's Party (ÖVP).
106	208	He was the European Union's Commissioner for Agriculture, Rural Development and Fisheries (1995–2004).
209	262	He also was President of the European Forum Alpbach.

262	327	Franz Fischler is married with Adelheid (Heidi) Hausmann in 1973.
328	408	They have two sons, Klaus and Georg and two daughters, Bernadette and Ursula.



408	589	Education and early career
Born in Absam, Tyrol Fischler studied agriculture at the University of Natural Resources and Applied Life Sciences Vienna, and finished as Dr rer.nat.oec.
590	598	in 1978.
599	740	He worked as University assistant from 1973 to 1979, then for the Tyrol Chamber of Agriculture, finally as its director from 1985 to 1989.



740	890	Political career

Between 1989 and 1994 Fischler was Federal Minister for Agriculture and Forestry, and since 1990 elected Member of National Council.
891	994	In 1995 he became European Commissioner in Brussels, responsible for agriculture and rural development.
995	1055	In 1999 fisheries also became part of his responsibilities.

1055	1137	At the 1999 Berlin summit, Fischler had significant influence on the Agenda 2000.

1137	1301	In 2011 Austria has decided to nominate Fischler as a candidate for the position of director general of FAO; the position went to José Graziano da Silva instead.



1301	1371	Other activities
Trilateral Commission, Member of the European Group.

1371	1488	Institute for Advanced Studies (IHS), Chair of the Board of Trustees


